{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862912-sidereals-where-fate-has-led-fan-project","id":862912,"title":"Sidereals: Where Fate Has Led (Fan Project)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-09T17:57:25-07:00","id":862912,"title":"Sidereals: Where Fate Has Led (Fan Project)","content":"I fucking love Sidereals!<br /> <br /> Thus, trying to take at least one stab at making them playable-ish without having to wait 6ish years.<br /> <br /> Sidereals: Where Fate Has Led is kind of an ongoing synthesis of my thoughts on how to Sidereal in Exalted 3e. It's also been instructive, in a 'look very closely at subsystems and Solar Charms, and see how the hooks that are placed are used'<br /> <br /> Still very much a work in progress; I'm through the Journeys and Serenity charms; next up- Battles!<br /> EDIT: Update! All 25 Abilities have at least a preliminary pass of charms! Next up- a brief break, and thence to Sidereal Astrological Projects!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1T4FTsSprLYd8KWXgE5Rr1x7C9_B6Ln5cnGN8HF7a3Vk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 04-21-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T13:18:08-07:00","id":869596,"title":"","content":"Cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Not so sure about having people spend xp to renounce their Kismet, though. xp costs like that rarely do anything good to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:57:13-07:00","id":869894,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of stressing the interrelations of the Maidens (the five-as-one goddess, as the Fates/Norns were three-as-one) by having four of the five Constellations per Caste be aligned with a second Maiden.<br /> <br /> I appreciate that you put Brawl back under the Gauntlet, in the house of Battles.<br /> <br /> I think that the Sword doesn't obviously tie into its associations and trappings, but it might if you clarify that Saturn's sword is not a combat weapon, but rather an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executioner%27s_sword\" target=\"_blank\">executioner's sword</a>. Something that brings a deliberate, sanctioned end to a doomed life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T03:51:12-07:00","id":870072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/862912-sidereals-where-fate-has-led-fan-project?p=869596#post869596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Not so sure about having people spend xp to renounce their Kismet, though. xp costs like that rarely do anything good to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My first pass was making it cost a permanent willpower. I want renouncing one's kismet to be an option, and a powerful and dramatic option at that- but one with such a high price it happens like, once a chronicle or is something an NPC does to up the stakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"useri